{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-928f6d614b1811abf5b5","statement":"One may try to define the internal convolution product $\\ostar$ on the whole $\\on{P}_{(L^+G)_{X^J}}(\\Gr_{X^J})$ using the same formula <<ref:internal convolution>>. However, the following example shows that $\\ostar$ is not perverse exact on this bigger category and this is one of the reasons we impose the ULA condition on the sheaves.\n\nAssume $G=\\{e\\}$ is trivial. Then $\\on{P}_{L^+G}(\\Gr_X)$ is nothing but the category of perverse sheaves on $X$ and $\\Sat_X$ is the category of local systems on $X$ shifted to degree $-1$. Then by definition,\n\n$$\\mA_1\\boxstar\\mA_2=\\mA_1\\boxtimes\\mA_2,\\quad \\mA_1\\ostar\\mA_2=\\mA_1\\otimes\\mA_2[-1].$$\n\nIn particular, if either $\\mA_1$ or $\\mA_2$ is a skyscraper sheaf, then $\\mA_1\\ostar\\mA_2$ is not perverse.","source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"c81ce78c1901216b7b0e57c8addead7316acb82cd89f864d9e8fd2c844685e04","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 175","ref_key":"triv group","name":"","order":212,"deps":[{"ref":"internal convolution","card_id":"ma-c-4f1f00c6b355972a6e46","label":"Equation internal convolution","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"9aa0de800bec9f56ae36a0522194f91bc11ab1fe49bff0d4068568a9eb549a68","line":2977,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T16:49:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":745,"math_hints":64}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","title":"Guide for Lecturers in the Park City Mathematics Institute","abstract":"We introduce various affine Grassmannians, study their geometric properties, and give some applications. We also discuss the geometric Satake equivalence. These are the expanded lecture no